
Gmail Email Delivery Setup

Copy the root .env.example file to .env and keep the real values out of version control.

DashDesk sends booking confirmations, reminder emails, and explicit chatbot follow-up emails through Gmail SMTP.

Required environment variables:

SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USERNAME=yourname@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your-16-character-gmail-app-password
SMTP_USE_TLS=true
SMTP_USE_SSL=false
MAIL_FROM=yourname@gmail.com
FLASK_SECRET_KEY=any-secure-random-string
ADMIN_KEY=your-admin-key

How to create the Gmail app password:
1. Turn on 2-Step Verification for the Gmail account.
2. Open Google Account > Security > App passwords.
3. Choose Mail and generate a 16-character app password.
4. Put that password in SMTP_PASSWORD in your local .env file and restart the Flask app.

What this app uses Gmail for:
- Booking confirmation emails after checkout.
- Upcoming and unpaid booking reminders.
- Explicit chatbot follow-up emails when the user asks to email the summary.

Useful endpoints:
- /api/email/send sends a mail message through the logged-in Gmail account.
- /chat can respond to booking questions and can also email a follow-up summary when the user asks for one.
- /api/admin/email-health shows whether Gmail SMTP is configured.

If Gmail does not deliver on the first try, check the Inbox, Spam, and Promotions folders, then confirm the app password and SMTP_HOST settings.